{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>You</b> [An Aramaic form], and these [are the explanations] — and behold, as though. [The word] אנת is Aramaic for 'you'; the verse means 'as though' one were seeing the image." "<b>This image</b> — this [is] a statue." "<b>Great</b> — large." "<b>And its radiance extraordinary</b> — perhaps it is like [the Hebrew month] Ziv [in which the word] זיו [appears]." "<b>And its appearance fearsome</b> — and its appearance [is] awesome."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:20.233191035Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}